.\"
.\" VFORK(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH VFORK 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
vfork \- create a child process and block parent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B pid_t vfork(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR vfork ()
is a variant of
.BR fork (2)
that is more efficient when the child will immediately call
.BR execve (2).
.PP
.BR vfork ()
differs from
.BR fork (2)
in that the calling thread is suspended until the child terminates
or calls
.BR execve ().
The child shares memory with its parent until that point.
.PP
.BR "CAUTION" :
The child must not return from the function calling
.BR vfork (),
and must not call any function other than
.BR _exit (2)
or one of the
.BR exec (3)
family before successfully calling one of those.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Same as
.BR fork (2).
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 66
.fi
.SS Recommendation
On modern systems with efficient COW fork implementation,
.BR fork (2)
is generally preferred over
.BR vfork ().
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (2),
.BR execve (2),
.BR _exit (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001 (marked OBSOLETE), POSIX.1-2008 (removed).
